{title: Our God}
{song_number: 134}
{language: en}
{artist: Matt Redman, Jonas Myrin, Chris Tomlin and Jesse Reeves}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Em]Water You [C]turned into [G]wine,
[Em]opened the [C]eyes of the [G]blind.
There's no one [Am]like You, none [Dsus4]like You.[D]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Em]Into the [C]darkness You [G]shine;
[Em]out of the [C]ashes we [G]rise.
There's no one [Am]like You, none [Dsus4]like You.[D]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Our God is [Em]greater, [C]our God is [D]stronger;
[G]God, You are higher than [D]any other.
[G]Our God is [Em]healer, [C]awesome in [D]power,
our [G]God, our God.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge}
[G]And if our God is [Dsus4]for us, [Em]then who could ever [C]stop us?
[G]And if our God is [Dsus4]with us, [Em]then what could stand a[C]gainst?
[G]What could stand against?
{end_of_bridge}
